---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import adam from '../assets/portfolio/creation-of-adam.jpg';
import { categoryUrl } from '../utils';
---

<section class="ai" id="portfolio" aria-labelledby="ai-heading">
  <div class="wrap ai__grid">
    <div class="ai__art">
      <!-- dark where it sits on the page ... -->
      <h2 class="heading ai__title" id="ai-heading">
        <span>AI</span><span>&amp;</span><span>Brain</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="ai__paint">
        <!-- Michelangelo, The Creation of Adam (c. 1512, public domain) -->
        <Image
          src={adam}
          alt="Michelangelo's The Creation of Adam: Adam reaching out to touch God's hand"
          widths={[700, 1100, 1600, 2000]}
          sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 55vw"
          class="ai__img"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <!-- ... and white where it sits on the painting: an identical copy, clipped to the painting -->
        <p class="heading ai__title ai__title--knock" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>AI</span><span>&amp;</span><span>Brain</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <p
        class="art-caption"
        data-note="If you look closely, what is behind God is a drawing of the brain. In this situation, the human symbolizes AI, and God symbolizes a brain, as we try to mimic only a part of nature."
      >
        * Michelangelo, <em>The Creation of Adam</em>, c. 1508–1512</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ai__text serif-text" data-reveal>
      <p>
        Do you think AI is smart? It is, but it isn't efficient. <span class="hl"
          >Training GPT-3 used as much energy as 370 human brains running for 20 years</span
        >. That's just training, and keeping it running will take more energy, land, water, and other resources.
      </p>
      <p>
        What I want is something that can help our planet, for example, <span class="hl" style="--hl-delay: 0.55s"
          >reverse-engineering our brain</span
        > to make AI better, safer, and more environmentally friendly.
      </p>
      <p>
        I've been implementing and studying Spiking Neural Networks (SNNs), which are a <span
          class="hl"
          style="--hl-delay: 0.95s">newer version of AI computation that mimics our neurons</span
        >.
      </p>
      <div class="ai__cta">
        <span>Interested?</span>
        <!-- the SNN capstone on the Research page: the same place its Pinned Items card goes -->
        <a class="btn-3d btn-3d--butter depth" href={`${categoryUrl('research')}#snn-capstone`}>Dive deeper</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .ai {
    background: var(--paper);
    padding: var(--sec-top) 0 var(--sec-bot);
  }

  .ai__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(32px, 5vw, 80px);
    /* "AI & BRAIN" starts level with the first line of the paragraph */
    align-items: start;
  }

  /* --ts: title size; --y: how far the painting starts below the title's top */
  .ai__art {
    --ts: clamp(2.4rem, 4.6vw, 4.4rem);
    --y: calc(var(--ts) * 0.42);
    position: relative;
  }

  .ai__title {
    font-size: var(--ts);
    line-height: 1;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75em;
    padding-left: 8%;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .ai__art > .ai__title {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0 0 auto 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  /* the painting, with a torn top edge where the plain plaster was cut away */
  .ai__paint {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    margin-top: var(--y);
    clip-path: polygon(
      0% 30%,
      7% 28.5%,
      15% 29.5%,
      23% 26%,
      31% 27.5%,
      39% 24%,
      46% 25%,
      52% 18%,
      56% 10%,
      61% 5%,
      66% 1.5%,
      74% 0%,
      100% 0%,
      100% 100%,
      0% 100%
    );
  }

  .ai__img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  /* the copy that shows on top of the painting, in the page colour */
  .ai__title--knock {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    top: calc(-1 * var(--y));
    color: var(--paper);
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .ai__text p {
    margin: 0 0 1em;
  }

  .ai__text p:first-child {
    margin-top: -0.25em; /* first line's cap height level with the title's */
  }

  .ai__cta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 14px 18px;
    margin-top: 1.6rem;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.3vw, 1.18rem);
  }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .ai__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    }
  }
</style>
